From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Ling <ling_kasim@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: drm/panel: chipone-icna35xx: enable DCS tearing effect (TE) signal

The ICNA35XX panel driver sends register 0x35 as a generic DSI write
(0x35, 0x00) but never issues the MIPI DCS SET_TEAR_ON command.  Every
other command-mode DSI panel driver in the tree calls
mipi_dsi_dcs_set_tear_on_multi(); without it the panel never drives its
TE output, the DPU tearcheck engine never sees a rising edge, and the
first framebuffer-console damage work item times out:

  msm_dpu ae01000.display-controller: vblank wait timed out on crtc 0
  dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_prepare_for_kickoff: failed wait_for_idle id:35 ret:-110 pp:0
  dpu_encoder_frame_done_timeout: enc35 frame done timeout

Add mipi_dsi_dcs_set_tear_on_multi(VBLANK) to both the ICNA3512 and
ICNA3520 init sequences, placed after exit_sleep_mode + 120 ms so the
panel is in normal mode before TE is configured.  The existing generic
0x35 write is retained in case it configures a Chipone-internal register
that is also needed.

Signed-off-by: Alex Ling <ling_kasim@hotmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c
@@ -109,6 +109,8 @@ static int icna3512_init_sequence(struct panel_info *pinfo)
 
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 120);
 
+	mipi_dsi_dcs_set_tear_on_multi(&dsi_ctx, MIPI_DSI_DCS_TEAR_MODE_VBLANK);
+
     mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x9F, 0x0F);
     mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xCE, 0x22);
 
@@ -178,6 +180,8 @@ static int icna3520_init_sequence(struct panel_info *pinfo)
 
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 120);
 
+	mipi_dsi_dcs_set_tear_on_multi(&dsi_ctx, MIPI_DSI_DCS_TEAR_MODE_VBLANK);
+
 	if (cur_vrefresh == 120) {
 		mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x48, 0x00);
 		mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x9F, 0x00);
